==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mega Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Mega Cat EX''' after being obtained from [[Cabaret Cat Awakens!]] and when at level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Similar to the [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] from the [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS]] banner, Cabaret Cat has vastly different stats between its Normal (spammable) and Evolved/[[True Form|True]] Forms (high performance), which have significantly different uses depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Very similar to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in terms of usage. Cheap and expendable, it can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, more important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of Cats able to perform this, usually with a lower cost. Cabaret Cat, however, can be used in {{4c}} stages, where there is considerably less competition. This is its only use. Even so, due to its higher than average cost, it's outclassed by any Basic Cat variant cheaper than it, such as [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]] and [[Coin Cat (Special Cat)|Coin Cat]].

==='''Evolved/True Form'''===
Despite the massive range gain, this unit remains mostly useless due to having subpar DPS with a very slow attack rate.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield|EvolvedClass = Super-Backliner|UltraClass=}}

